@lang en
-- Source text: Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland), Act No. 23 of 2005, as enacted, from the unofficial plain-text rendering No.-23-of-2005.txt.
-- (c) Government of Ireland. Oireachtas Copyright Material is reproduced with the permission of the Houses of the Oireachtas.
--
-- THESE ARE NOT THE ACT'S ANSWERS.
-- This module holds the alternative readings that the Interpretation Act 2005 does NOT adopt, so that the fork register in NOTES.md can show,
-- by running them, what each reading would answer for the worked cases.
-- Nothing in ie-interpretation-time.l4 calls anything here; the Act's own module refuses where the text is silent.
--
-- Why each is a reading and not the text:
--   B (corresponding date, clamped to the last day of a shorter month): the Act contains no rule that a month or a year ends on a "corresponding date".
--   C (corresponding date, rolled into the next month): the same silence; and `Date` rolls where `YMD` refuses.
--   D (a week from any day is seven days): the Schedule defines "week" only as the period between midnight on a Saturday and midnight on the following Saturday.
--   Rest-day roll forward: the Act contains no provision that moves a last day.
-- Whoever relies on one of these relies on a rule from outside the text, which this run was told not to import.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`

§ `Reading B: the corresponding date, clamped to the last day of a shorter month`

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177); the Act has no corresponding-date rule
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reading B: the corresponding date` n `calendar months after` d MEANS
    IF   `n is a whole number of at least one` n
    THEN `add months` d n
    ELSE `a period must be a whole number of units, at least one`

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177); the Act has no corresponding-date rule
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reading B: the corresponding date` n `years after` d MEANS
    IF   `n is a whole number of at least one` n
    THEN `add years` d n
    ELSE `a period must be a whole number of units, at least one`

-- Variant B-inclusive: s 18(h) includes the first day, so a period of N months from D would end on the day BEFORE the corresponding date.
-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177); the Act has no corresponding-date rule
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reading B, first day included: the last day of` n `calendar months from` d MEANS
    (`reading B: the corresponding date` n `calendar months after` d) MINUS 1

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177); the Act has no corresponding-date rule
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reading B, first day included: the last day of` n `years from` d MEANS
    (`reading B: the corresponding date` n `years after` d) MINUS 1

§ `Reading C: the corresponding date, rolled into the next month when the month is short`

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177); the Act has no corresponding-date rule
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reading C: the corresponding date` n `calendar months after` d MEANS
    IF   `n is a whole number of at least one` n
    THEN Date (DATE_DAY d) ((DATE_MONTH d) PLUS n) (DATE_YEAR d)
    ELSE `a period must be a whole number of units, at least one`

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177); the Act has no corresponding-date rule
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reading C: the corresponding date` n `years after` d MEANS
    IF   `n is a whole number of at least one` n
    THEN Date (DATE_DAY d) (DATE_MONTH d) ((DATE_YEAR d) PLUS n)
    ELSE `a period must be a whole number of units, at least one`

§ `Reading D: a period of N weeks from any day is seven times N days`

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
-- src:245 | “week” means the period between midnight on any Saturday and midnight on the following Saturday;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h); Schedule Pt 1 "week" (src:177, src:245)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`reading D: the last day of` n `weeks from any day` d MEANS
    `the last day of a period of` (7 TIMES n) `days beginning on or reckoned from` d

§ `Reading R: a last day on a day of rest, recess or holiday rolls forward to the next day that is not one`

-- src:177 | (h) Periods of time. Where a period of time is expressed to begin on or be reckoned from a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period and, where a period of time is expressed to end on or be reckoned to a particular day, that day shall be deemed to be included in the period;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(h) (src:177); no provision of the text moves a last day
GIVEN d      IS A DATE
      `rest days` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
      fuel   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`reading R: the next day that is not a day of rest, recess or holiday, on or after` d `, rest days being` `rest days` `, searching` fuel `days at most` MEANS
    BRANCH IF fuel AT MOST 0 THEN `no day was found within the search limit`
           IF `rest days` d   THEN `reading R: the next day that is not a day of rest, recess or holiday, on or after` (d PLUS 1) `, rest days being` `rest days` `, searching` (fuel MINUS 1) `days at most`
           OTHERWISE d
